## 1. Product Scope and Architecture

### 1.1 Product goals

ironLog is a straightforward workout tracker for one person. It should
make it easy to:

- Browse and search exercises.
- Create custom exercises.
- Create and manage workout routines.
- Start and log workouts.
- Resume an interrupted workout.
- Track workout history.
- Review exercise-specific history and personal records.
- See basic workout statistics.
- Export and restore all app data.

### 1.2 Platform scope

Supported:

- iOS
- Android

Explicitly unsupported for this MVP:

- Web
- Desktop
- Multi-user accounts
- Cross-device synchronisation

### 1.3 Core architecture

The app consists of:

- Expo + React Native user interface.
- TypeScript domain logic.
- Zod validation.
- A central repository responsible for application data.
- One app-managed JSON document stored in private application storage.
- Import/export functionality for user-managed backups.

There is no server and no network dependency for core functionality.

### 1.4 Architecture diagram

```text
             Expo / React Native UI
                       |
                       v
                 Domain layer
       Workouts / Exercises / Routines / PRs
                       |
                       v
                 Data repository
      State / Validation / Persistence / Backup
                       |
                       v
              Local JSON document
             ironlog-data.json
```

UI components must not read or write the JSON file directly. All data
access goes through the repository.

