## 7. Persistence and Application Lifecycle

Local workout persistence is a core requirement.

Requirements:

- An active workout survives navigation.
- An active workout survives app suspension.
- An active workout survives app restart.
- Changes are saved frequently enough that normal interruption does
  not lose meaningful work.
- Important actions trigger immediate persistence.
- Failed writes never cause local state loss.
- On startup, detect and offer to resume an active workout.
- Clear or mark the active workout completed only after the completed
  state has been successfully persisted.
- Explicit discard removes the active workout only after the deletion
  has been successfully persisted.

There is no network state and no server recovery path.

